are of revenue (1.15x).","It accounts for 0.9% of sector revenue and 1.0% of sector operating profit.","Over five years it has been losing share of the sector profit pool (-6.3% a year).","The sector is fragmented and competitive (HHI 0.03 across 377 companies in the universe; the top four hold 26% of revenue), so pricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares are in a steep downtrend, down 45% over the past year excluding the latest month.","The price sits near the bottom of its 52-week range, 45% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 36% and a beta of 1.00, it moves roughly with the market.","Liquidity is deep, with about $1.1B traded a day.","In past sell-offs it fell 40% in the 2020 crash, 50% in the 2022 bear market and 44% in 2008."],"val":["The price sits above its DCF fair value of $33.67 (margin of safety -13%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 20%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $25.37 to $45.56 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Consumer Cyclical peers: P/FCF 25.8 vs 16.7 (sector median).","Against its own history it is cheap: the EBIT multiple sits 40% below its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 3.9% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 7.2% (vs the 8% bar).","The 38 covering analysts target $36.46 on average, 4% below the price."],"prof":["ROIC of 34% clears the cost of capital of 8.9% by 25pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.32).","It runs a 45% gross margin and converts 5% of revenue into free cash flow.","ROE of 21% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.6x equity multiplier).","It spends 1.5% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is conservative at 0.1x net debt to EBITDA ($7.6B of cash against $7.9B of debt), with interest covered 13.1x.","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 3.4, in the safe zone).","Its debt comes due soon (maturity wall about 1.8 years out), so refinancing terms matter."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at -3.2% over 3 years, 0.8% over 5 years and 3.7% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating.","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded -18.2% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (0.9x, 1.5% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 4, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business.","It has beaten earnings estimates by 135.5% on average."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 1.9%, and institutions hold 85%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (7 sales, net $669K sold).","It returns 4.5% a year to shareholders (0.3% in buybacks and 4.3% in dividends).","The share count has grown 1.6% a year over five years, diluting existing holders.","It has paid a dividend for 38 consecutive years, raising it 8.0% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 73,000 employees, each generates about $636K of revenue, 1.7x the Consumer Cyclical median, and revenue has grown 5.7% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $30K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $4.2M (7x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores poorly (10/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $10K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":61,"head":"Watch: composite 45, above the 39 line, but no margin of safety; it becomes a buy below $28.62.","pros":["Composite 45, above the 39 line (gates 11/26)","ROIC 33.8% vs WACC 8.9%","Net debt/EBITDA 0.1x","Altman Z in the safe zone","Returns 4.5% a year to shareholders"],"cons":["Trades 13% above fair value of $33.67","P/FCF 25.8x vs sector 16.7x","12-1 month momentum -45%"],"flags":[],"need":["no margin of safety"],"buy_below":28.62,"vc":{"base":33.67,"base_src":"dcf","bear":25.37,"bull":45.56,"alt_median":31